From 665979bb50809e6e5139405d405d5e68bcf5612c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glib Shpychka <23005347+gshpychka@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:25:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Support the kitty clipboard protocol (OSC 5522) with paste
 events

Panes can turn on paste events (mode 5522) and read or write the client
terminal's clipboard with OSC 5522, as the protocol's section on
multiplexers describes:
https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/clipboard/#support-for-terminal-multiplexers

tmux detects support with a DECRQM query for mode 5522 (feature
"osc5522"). It sets the mode on the client terminal while the active pane
has it and no prompt or overlay takes input. Paste events carry no id and
go to the active pane.

A pane's read or write goes to the most recently active client with the
feature, under an id of tmux's own. Replies with that id return to the
pane with the pane's id restored. One request is in flight at a time;
another gets EBUSY, and ENOSYS when no client has the feature. A request
ends on DONE, an error status, the client's exit, or 30 seconds without a
packet.
